# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# --- The database -----------------------------------------------------------
# app.db is generated, not authored. schema.sql builds it, the migrate_*.py
# scripts evolve it and seed_demo_data.py fills it with fictional demo data, so all
# three of those ARE tracked and the database itself is not. See README.md for
# how to rebuild it after a fresh clone.
app.db
# Point-in-time copies taken before anything that rewrites existing rows. They
# are kept on the machine as the recovery path for that change, and are excluded
# here for the same reason app.db is -- plus they hold real patient records,
# which do not belong in version control at all.
#
# This was `app.db.PRETASK_BACKUP_*` until a cleanup pass took a backup named
# `app.db.PRECLEANUP_BACKUP_...` and git offered to commit it. The rule this
# stanza states has always been about what the file *contains*, not what it is
# called, so a pattern keyed to one naming convention was a hole waiting for the
# first backup that did not use it. Any copy of the database is a copy of the
# database.
#
# Deliberately `app.db.*` and not `app.db*`: the sidecar files below are
# hyphenated (`app.db-wal`), and they are listed separately because they are
# excluded for a different reason -- a half-written transaction, not patient
# data. Two reasons, two rules, so neither can be deleted on the strength of the
# other.
app.db.*
# SQLite's sidecar files. They exist only while a connection is open, and a
# committed one would be a half-written transaction.
app.db-journal
app.db-wal
app.db-shm

# --- Verification screenshots -----------------------------------------------
# Screenshots taken while click-testing a feature in a real browser. They are
# kept on the machine as evidence a thing was actually exercised, and they are
# excluded here for the SAME reason the database backups above are: a screenshot
# of the Patient Profile is a patient record. The ones from the vaccination
# correction pass carry a full name, a patient ID, an age, a home address, a
# contact number and a clinical history, which is more identifying material than
# a row of app.db holds, not less -- the file format is different and the data is
# the same. A repository that refuses to hold app.db must refuse to hold a
# picture of app.db.
#
# The folder itself is tracked, and so is its README, so the evidence is
# discoverable by anyone who needs it and its absence from git is stated rather
# than left to be discovered. See docs/verification/README.md.
docs/verification/**/*.jpg
docs/verification/**/*.jpeg
docs/verification/**/*.png
docs/verification/**/*.gif
docs/verification/**/*.webp

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# config.py reads SECRET_KEY from the environment and refuses to start without one.
# A real key belongs in a .env that never leaves the machine.
.env
*.env
# Other environment files, such as .env.local.
.env.*
# The template with names only and no values is tracked on purpose.
!.env.example

# --- More guards for patient data (added 2026-09-28) ------------------------
# Any SQLite database file, anywhere in the project. Only schema.sql is tracked.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Any copy of a database file (app.db.PRETASK_BACKUP_..., test.db.old, ...).
*.db.*
# Backup copies by name, and a backups folder.
# Not "*BACKUP*": git here ignores case, so that would also hide
# models/backup.py and any new source file with "backup" in its name.
*_BACKUP_*
backups/
# Source files are never backups, whatever their name.
!*.py
!*.html
!*.sql
!*.md
# Other common names for a virtual environment folder.
venv/
env/
# The tests do not write into the project. Each suite uses its own folder in
# the system temp folder (see tests/_support.py), so no tests/ rule is needed.

# --- Tooling and scratch work -----------------------------------------------
.claude/
# Nothing of the sort is in the project today -- verification scripts have been
# kept outside it deliberately -- but this is where they would land if anyone
# ever wrote one in place.
scratchpad/
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Everything else is tracked on purpose: app.py, config.py, schema.sql, every
# migrate_*.py, seed_demo_data.py, requirements.txt, and the whole of
# routes/ models/ utils/ database/ templates/ static/ PR0MPT_INSTRUCTION/.
# static/ in particular is vendored on purpose -- Bootstrap, Chart.js and the
# Inter/Material fonts are committed so the app runs with no network at all.

# --- Error log (Task 10) --------------------------------------------------------
# Error traces can quote what a person typed, so they stay on this computer.
logs/

# --- HTTPS certificate and key (network mode) ---------------------------------
# setup_https.py writes them to instance/certs/. A private key in git would let anyone
# with the code read the health center's network traffic. The file types are ignored
# everywhere too, as a second guard.
instance/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
